## Appendix A The Influence of the He Background

The instrumental background of _Insight_-HXMT/HE is mainly related to its attitude and the orbit. We performed many simulations by assuming random reference times to extract lightcurves from raw events of actual observations, as we did with real bursts' time. We found that despite averaging 73 lightcurves, the long-term variability of the background could not be fully mitigated. In Figure 1, we show a representative example of averaged lightcurves which exhibits a downward trend.

In addition, we also tested the downward trend by analyzing a sample of bursts observed during low-background orbits. This sample comprises 12 bursts, for which we were able to estimate the background using the official tool _hebkgmap_ and generate an averaged lightcurve with background subtraction (shown in Figure 2). Clearly, the hard X-ray deficit is still significant around the burst peak, while the overall downward trend disappears. This concludes that the downward trend shown in Figure 1 is likely due to an average change of the instrumental background.